{"author":{"id":"973fc03426eba9a243913e0f6e6823e102397744f60a9ab11c882af948c310c4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1778519688,"nonce":"Dsa4Eeaol2Y8WwA+Sl3RtmkEJ5Y=","title":"Scoped auth-result delivery via MCP channel + tiered escalation","message":"## Goal\n\nReplace the current \"every session dumps every inbox auth_result on every prompt\" UX with a scoped, channel-delivered model:\n\n- **Tier 1** (default): an auth_result is delivered only to the session that submitted the request, via the MCP channel server, in real time when the session is alive. Delivery marks the item as `delivered` — no further surfacing.\n- **Tier 2**: if the owning session never returned to receive delivery, after a configurable grace (default **7 days**) surface to any session in the same project on session start.\n- **Tier 3**: if still nothing, after a longer grace (default **30 days**) surface to any session globally on session start.\n\nConcretely fixes `b47891b` (inbox ack not scoped to session), implements a piece of `4aa3e17` (session orchestrator for async event delivery), and slots under `c58acc8` (user-configurable Mandible policies) for the grace settings.\n\nSurfaced from rlrmp session; cross-ref on rlrmp `1d9ae6f`.\n\n## Current state\n\nThe `channel-server/` MCP server is **already built** (2026-03-20, six TS files). It:\n- Subscribes to Mandible SSE at `/api/events`\n- Forwards `auth:resolved`, `auth:completed`, `inbox:updated`, `work_unit:*` events as MCP notifications\n- Registers its session with Mandible on startup (`client.registerSession`)\n- Has reconnect/backoff logic\n\nWhat's missing:\n\n1. **No session scoping on `auth:resolved`**: the 10 emission sites in `src/auth-queue.ts` broadcast to all SSE consumers. Any channel server connected sees the event regardless of which session submitted the originating request.\n2. **No `delivered_at` state**: there is currently only \"acknowledged\". Items sit in the inbox until a session explicitly acks (which any session in the same dir can do — `b47891b`).\n3. **No tiered escalation**: items are either acked (gone) or unacked (everyone sees them forever).\n4. **The inbox-dump hook fires every turn**: `~/.dotfiles/.config/claude/settings.json` registers `mandible-inbox-check.sh` on `UserPromptSubmit` (not `SessionStart`). The dump fires on every prompt the user types. Immediate pain point.\n5. **No MCP wiring**: `~/.dotfiles/.config/claude/settings.json` has no `mcpServers` entry registering the channel server, so it is not currently running for live Claude Code sessions.\n6. **No grace settings**: defaults to be added per `c58acc8`.\n\n## Design\n\n### Data model\n\nAdd to the `auth_request` (or `auth_result`) table:\n- `target_session_id TEXT` — the session that submitted the request (NULL = legacy / unowned)\n- `target_repo_root TEXT` — the project root for Tier 2 scoping\n- `delivered_at INTEGER` — epoch ms when channel pushed the notification (NULL = undelivered)\n\n`mandible auth request` (CLI) writes both new fields at submission time, sourcing `MANDIBLE_SESSION_ID` from the environment and `repo_root` from the current worktree → main worktree mapping.\n\n### Event scoping\n\nThe SSE event `auth:resolved` payload gains `target_session_id`. The channel server (`channel-server/notifications.ts`) compares to its own `MANDIBLE_SESSION_ID`:\n\n- **match** → forward MCP notification AND call new endpoint `POST /api/inbox/delivered/\u003cauth_request_id\u003e` which marks `delivered_at`. Mandible then stops surfacing the item.\n- **mismatch** → drop. Do not notify other sessions.\n- **`target_session_id == null`** (legacy / unscoped) → keep current broadcast behaviour for safety.\n\n### Inbox API (`src/routes/inbox.ts`)\n\nUpdate the `auth_results` query in `GET /api/inbox`:\n\n- **Tier 1**: `target_session_id = $current_session_id AND delivered_at IS NULL`\n- **Tier 2**: `target_session_id != $current_session_id AND target_repo_root = $current_repo_root AND delivered_at IS NULL AND resolved_at \u003c (now - project_grace_days)`\n- **Tier 3**: `target_repo_root != $current_repo_root AND delivered_at IS NULL AND resolved_at \u003c (now - global_grace_days)`\n\nUnion sorted by tier ascending. Tier 1 should be empty in practice when channel push is working; it acts as a fallback for sessions without a channel attached.\n\n### Hooks\n\n- **`hooks/session-start.sh`** (Mandible): replace dump-everything with a call to the scoped inbox API. Output one summary line if anything is present, nothing otherwise.\n- **`~/.dotfiles/.config/claude/settings.json`** (separate dotfiles change after this merges):\n  - Move `mandible-inbox-check.sh` from `UserPromptSubmit` to `SessionStart` (or remove entirely — its job is now done by `session-start.sh`).\n  - Add `mcpServers.mandible` registration pointing at `channel-server/dist/index.js`.\n\n### Settings\n\nAdd to Mandible settings DB (per `c58acc8`):\n- `inbox.project_grace_days` default `7`\n- `inbox.global_grace_days` default `30`\n\nSettings UI affordance is out-of-scope here — backend settings are sufficient.\n\n### Backward compatibility\n\nRows lacking `target_session_id` (pre-migration) keep current behaviour until they age out via natural ack or the 30-day global grace. No data migration beyond column adds.\n\n### No ack required\n\nChannel delivery is the ack. We do not require the agent to call back with an explicit acknowledgement — the `delivered_at` write from the channel server is the durable record. (A future audit hook could attach `Bug:` trailers from subsequent commits to close the loop, but it's not needed.)\n\n## Deliverables (Mandible-side; this issue)\n\n1. **Schema migration**: add three columns to the auth_request/auth_result table.\n2. **`src/auth-queue.ts`**: populate `target_session_id`/`target_repo_root` on insert; include `target_session_id` in all `auth:resolved` event payloads (10 sites).\n3. **New endpoint**: `POST /api/inbox/delivered/\u003cauth_request_id\u003e` marks `delivered_at`; returns 204. Idempotent.\n4. **`src/routes/inbox.ts`**: rewrite the `auth_results` query with tier logic + grace-settings lookup.\n5. **Settings**: add the two grace fields with defaults.\n6. **`channel-server/notifications.ts`**: filter on `target_session_id`, call the delivered endpoint, drop foreign events.\n7. **CLI — `mandible auth request`**: pass `MANDIBLE_SESSION_ID` and repo root in the POST body.\n8. **`hooks/session-start.sh`**: rewrite to scoped summary.\n9. **Tests** (vitest): tier query, delivered endpoint, channel-server filter, CLI submission populating new fields.\n\n## Deferred to a follow-up dotfiles issue\n\n10. **`~/.dotfiles/.config/claude/settings.json`**:\n    - Move `mandible-inbox-check.sh` registration from `UserPromptSubmit` to `SessionStart` (or delete).\n    - Add `mcpServers.mandible` stdio entry pointing at the built channel server.\n    - Goes through the dotfiles auth-request workflow once this Mandible work merges.\n\n## Out of scope (file as separate issues if/when needed)\n\n- Settings UI for grace periods (backend is enough for now).\n- Importance pinning (`f6d972a`).\n- Continuation-item scoping (covers `auth_result` items only; continuations may want similar treatment but the design differs).\n- Auth-request TTL / duplicate prevention (`c3e0aa6`).\n\n## Cross-refs\n\n- Builds on / partially implements `4aa3e17`\n- Fixes `b47891b`\n- Lives under `c58acc8` (for the two new settings)\n- Channel-server foundation `1d652d5`\n- rlrmp meta coord cross-ref: `1d9ae6f`","files":null}]}